\tag{changelog}
\tag{stdlib}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1041}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|std::regex::alphabet::utf8~} turns a \code{\verb~|CharSet~} into the UTF-8 encodings of its members: \code{\verb~|fold_sequences~} feeds a function the sequences of one to four byte ranges, \code{\verb~|Utf8Sequence~} and \code{\verb~|Utf8Range~}, in the order of the bytes. A matcher over bytes needs them to match text. See [the translation](design-regex-derivatives-utf8). \pr{1041}.}
